div.p:
—The notion, however, that only the USSR benefits from détente is wrong. U.S.
                    failures in Asia and its difficulties along NATO’s southern flank are not the
                    USSR’s fault but are due to cold war policies;

—The USSR did not pledge to guarantee the social status quo in the world and to
                    halt the process of national liberation as part of détente; however, the USSR
                    does not regard détente as an instrument for “nudging forward” this process;
